# .NET build output inside C# test fixtures. MSBuild stamps the repository's own HEAD into
# AssemblyInformationalVersionAttribute, so these files change on every commit and can never be
# stable in the repo that produces them. No test reads them: the fixtures are copied file-by-file
# into t.TempDir(), and the one whole-tree copy rsyncs with --exclude obj.
#
# NOTE: internal/evaluator/apisurface/testdata/cs_repo/bin/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Its
# Microsoft.Playwright.xml is a real fixture — apisurface/csharp_test.go asserts on
# api.Origin == "Microsoft.Playwright.xml" — so a wildcard **/bin/ or **/obj/ rule would delete it
# and break that test. Keep these rules path-specific.
internal/testbootstrap/testdata/csharp_csproj_bare/obj/
internal/testbootstrap/testdata/e2e_csharp_playwright/obj/
internal/testbootstrap/testdata/csharp_aspnetcore_no_test_project/**/obj/
internal/testbootstrap/testdata/csharp_aspnetcore_no_test_project/**/bin/

# Generated patches / scratch
*.patch
/tmp/
